WEBVTT

00:19:59.708 --> 00:20:02.476
or you didn't share with the person
how that bothered you.

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:05.768
There are really nice ways, polite ways

00:20:05.792 --> 00:20:09.518
to still communicate
a really powerful, emotional point.

00:20:09.542 --> 00:20:12.059
AG: It was a huge realization for Alexi.

00:20:12.083 --> 00:20:15.226
Up until then, he'd been
bottling up these issues in his head,

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:18.643
convinced that he needed
to solve all his problems on his own

00:20:18.667 --> 00:20:21.226
because he thought
that's what strong leaders do.

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:23.059
AR: And I think that's the great lie.

00:20:23.083 --> 00:20:26.059
I think any great human
who's accomplished anything

00:20:26.083 --> 00:20:28.809
had an ecosystem
of people supporting them.

00:20:28.833 --> 00:20:31.101
AG: Alexi knew
that pro athletes and actors